          "name": "Bird Jesus (Normal)",
          "pokemon": "Pidgeot",
          "shiny": false,
          "gender": "DC",
          "levels": [],
          "description": "<p><a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/pidgeot-mega/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mega Pidgeot</a> is one of the premier special attackers Normal teams have access to because of its good Speed tier and a powerful, coveted STAB move in Hurricane that beats nuisances to Normal teams like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/kommo-o/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Kommo-o</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/ogerpon-wellspring/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Ogerpon-W</a> while never missing. Heat Wave complements Hurricane well by heavily damaging Steel-types like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/jirachi/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Jirachi</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/ferrothorn/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Ferrothorn</a>, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/scizor-mega/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mega Scizor</a>, which makes Mega Pidgeot very effective against Psychic, Grass, and Bug teams. Roost heightens Mega Pidgeot's longevity by taking advantage of defensive Pokemon that can't hit it very hard, such as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/sableye-mega/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mega Sableye</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/slowbro/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Slowbro</a>. In the last slot, Toxic's ability to cripple switch-ins like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/iron-hands/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Iron Hands</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/rotom-wash/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Rotom-W</a>, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/mantine/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mantine</a> is preferred, but U-turn is valuable to keep momentum and flee from checks such as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/heatran/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Heatran</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/muk-alola/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Alolan Muk</a>. <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/ursaluna/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Ursaluna</a> forms an incredible wallbreaking core with Mega Pidgeot; it is able to demolish special walls like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/clodsire/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Clodsire</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/goodra-hisui/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Hisuian Goodra</a> and can switch into Electric-type moves that target the bird. In return, Mega Pidgeot helps Ursaluna beat physical walls like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/venusaur-mega/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mega Venusaur</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/skarmory/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Skarmory</a>, revenge kills Grass- and Fighting-types such as Ogerpon-W and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/keldeo/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Keldeo</a> that threaten the bear, and is able to U-turn into Ursaluna so it activates its Flame Orb safely. <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/staraptor/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Staraptor</a> is a great defensive pivot that removes entry hazards for Mega Pidgeot and brings it into the field unscathed with U-turn. Similarly, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/chansey/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Chansey</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/blissey/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Blissey</a>, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/porygon2/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Porygon2</a> are very bulky partners that can switch into most attacks aimed at Mega Pidgeot and pivot into it via Teleport. Chansey and Blissey also lay down Stealth Rock to help Mega Pidgeot net more KOs, notably letting it OHKO Mega Venusaur and 2HKO <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/toxapex/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Toxapex</a> with Hurricane.</p>",
